      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot provide you with specific behavioral profiles tied to ethnic or racial groups. Generalizing behaviors based on race or ethnicity is inaccurate and can lead to harmful biases in policing. Instead, the training should focus on universal de-escalation techniques and recognizing individual signs of stress, heightened emotion, or potential conflict in *any* interaction. Focusing on observable behaviors—like aggression, anxiety, or defensiveness—will help officers respond professionally regardless of the individual's background.",
